Solve room pressures together with the flow network (@cm-network-balance: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @clean-manufacturing, #source "../sources/CONTAM-Multizone-Airflow-and-Contaminants-NIST.lingua#r_5HECDC480RSYAJ3SQ2QNFHCN46", #clean-manufacturing "Work-a-two-room-pressure-and-transfer-example.lingua#r_07JAMYKSV9JJ9RVBA1DRDNBGHT") { r_607YQN6PMG03XAQPK8W65S7G3V
**Read:** [Multizone airflow and contaminants — Dols and Polidoro, CONTAM 3.4](../sources/CONTAM-Multizone-Airflow-and-Contaminants-NIST.lingua#r_5HECDC480RSYAJ3SQ2QNFHCN46), chapter 8.3.1–8.3.3 and its numerical formulation.

At steady state each zone conserves air mass. For a constant-density approximation, imposed supply minus exhaust equals net flow leaving through its connecting paths. Shared paths must have equal and opposite contributions at their endpoints. Fix a pressure reference before solving.

Nonlinear path relations make room pressures coupled unknowns. The numerical residual is the unbalanced flow at each zone, not merely the change between two successive pressure guesses. A disconnected network without a reference can leave an undetermined pressure.

**Work:** Assemble a two-room network with outdoor paths and one connecting path. Check total building balance by summing the two equations. Solve it first with linear conductances, then a declared power law. Compare an independently computed residual and perturb an exhaust demand before trusting a displayed pressure map.

**Return:** [Clean manufacturing and contamination control — from familiar objects to controlled processes](../Clean-manufacturing-and-contamination-control.lingua#r_7D8SQ8BVQDZQBDBGC6DP0JAMZN).
